<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alanya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alaiye, Kalonoros</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alanya is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. The Byzantine town of Kalonoros was taken in 1221 by the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayqubad-i">Kayqubad I</a>, who renamed it Alaiye and made it a winter residence and naval base, building its citadel walls, the Red Tower and a shipyard. It later passed to local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beyliks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took it in 1471.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alanya.jpg" alt="Alanya" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ozgurmulazimoglu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alanyafromcastle.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
